<title>BELGIUM: TABLE-BELGIAN MONEY MARKET SUPPLY CUT IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>TABLE-BELGIAN MONEY MARKET SUPPLY CUT IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said</p>
<p>it withdrew liquidity from the money market in the week to July</p>
<p>14. Forex reserves rose due to quarterly Ecus swap with EMI</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   452.162 (+ 3.906)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  22.920 (+ 5.157)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.324 (- 0.012)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   25.795 (- 0.000)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 115.561 (- 6.195)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   482.834 (- 1.506)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
